cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use bmassa, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "bmassa: Biomass of Aquatic Taxa from Abundances and Body Sizes"
version: 0.6.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/STABLE-uv/bmassa"
authors:
  - family-names: "Amador Crespo"
    given-names: "Pablo"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3793-8794"
  - family-names: "Rico"
    given-names: "Andreu"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1820-4218"
abstract: >-
  R package that estimates the mean individual mass and the biomass of
  aquatic taxa (phytoplankton, zooplankton, macroinvertebrates, fish and
  amphibians) from abundance data, with prediction intervals from
  hierarchical models fitted along the taxonomy, and converts them to other
  currencies, among them energy.
keywords:
  - R
  - biomass
  - body mass
  - length-mass relationships
  - freshwater ecology
  - food webs
